# Better Auth with Next.js: Key Integration Patterns

## Server-Side Session Retrieval

To access the session in a server component, use the `auth.api.getSession()` method with Next.js headers:

```tsx
import { auth } from "@/lib/auth"
import { headers } from "next/headers"

export async function ServerComponent() {
    const session = await auth.api.getSession({
        headers: await headers()
    })
    if(!session) {
        return <div>Not authenticated</div>
    }
    return <div>Welcome {session.user.name}</div>
}
```

## Server Action Cookies with nextCookies Plugin

When using server actions that modify cookies (like `signInEmail`), you need the `nextCookies` plugin. Per the documentation, this plugin "must be the last plugin in the array" since it automatically handles Set-Cookie headers:

```ts
import { betterAuth } from "better-auth";
import { nextCookies } from "better-auth/next-js";

export const auth = betterAuth({
    plugins: [nextCookies()] // Last position required
})
```

Then cookies are automatically set during server actions:

```ts
"use server";
const signIn = async () => {
    await auth.api.signInEmail({
        body: { email: "user@email.com", password: "password" }
    })
}
```

## Route Protection Approaches

**Cookie-based check (optimistic):**
```ts
import { getSessionCookie } from "better-auth/cookies";

export async function middleware(request: NextRequest) {
    const sessionCookie = getSessionCookie(request);
    if (!sessionCookie) {
        return NextResponse.redirect(new URL("/sign-in", request.url));
    }
    return NextResponse.next();
}
```

**Full validation (Next.js 15.2.0+ with Node.js runtime):**
```ts
import { auth } from "@/lib/auth";

export async function middleware(request: NextRequest) {
    const session = await auth.api.getSession({
        headers: await headers()
    })
    if(!session) {
        return NextResponse.redirect(new URL("/sign-in", request.url));
    }
    return NextResponse.next();
}

export const config = {
    runtime: "nodejs",
    matcher: ["/dashboard"]
};
```

**Next.js 16+ proxy approach:**
Rename `middleware.ts` to `proxy.ts` and change the function name accordingly; all Better Auth methods work identically.

